[E0341] Error: a `lend fn` lends a place, and its result is `&T`
    ╭─[ err/187_lend_fn/main.wip:14:21 ]
    │
 14 │     lend fn size(): i64 = 3
    │                     ─┬─  
    │                      ╰─── not a `&` reference
    │ 
    │ Note: `lend fn` declares a projection's reading half and its writing half from one body: the result is `&T` where the call reads and `&var T` where it writes
────╯
[E0341] Error: a `lend fn` lends a place, and its result is `&T`
    ╭─[ err/187_lend_fn/main.wip:17:20 ]
    │
 17 │     lend fn raw(): &var i64 = lend self.x
    │                    ────┬───  
    │                        ╰───── written `&var`
    │ 
    │ Help: write `&`: the writing half lends it as `&var` by itself
    │ 
    │ Note: `lend fn` declares a projection's reading half and its writing half from one body: the result is `&T` where the call reads and `&var T` where it writes
────╯
[E0418] Error: a `lend fn` lends a place its writing half cannot write
    ╭─[ err/187_lend_fn/main.wip:20:33 ]
    │
 20 │     lend fn view(): &i64 = lend self.fixed()
    │                                 ──────┬─────  
    │                                       ╰─────── only ever read
    │ 
    │ Help: declare it `fn`: what it lends is for reading only
    │ 
    │ Note: `lend fn` is checked twice, once reading and once writing, and each must lend what it names
────╯
